  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday Night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1145 PM CDT Wed Sep 30 2026\n\nPrecipitation will be ongoing Thursday evening across parts of\nsoutheast Oklahoma into northwest Arkansas. As the upper low lift\nnortheastward away from the area, a cold front will be forced\nsouthward Thursday evening into Friday. Scattered showers and\nstorms remain possible along the boundary across northeast\nOklahoma Thursday evening and then shifting into southeast\nOklahoma on Friday and into the weekend. Cooler, more Fall like\ntemperatures will follow in the wake of the boundary on Friday,\nalong with breezy northerly winds adding a little more chill to\nthe air.\n\nThe elongated mid level trough axis will linger in the vicinity\ninto Saturday. The result will be continued chances for showers,\nmainly across southeast Oklahoma into west central Arkansas. Any\nadditional rain should be fairly light by this time. Another weak\nmid level wave will drop southeastward across eastern Oklahoma on\nSunday, bringing another chance for a few showers Sunday morning\nacross southeast Oklahoma, before exiting the area by afternoon.\nSurface high pressure will settle over the region through the\nearly part of next week with cooler and drier pleasant conditions\nprevailing for several days to finish out the period.\n\nBowlan",
